# SRG-APP-000168-AU-002510  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to enforce password complexity
# by requiring that at least one numeric character be used.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000168-AU-002510
group:           V-206471
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk's native authentication can require a minimum number of numeric
                 characters in every password it accepts.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordDigit min 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordDigit https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where authType is LDAP or SAML, password complexity for federated accounts
                 is enforced by the directory service or identity provider; [splunk_auth]
                 governs the remaining native accounts
external:        Operating system account passwords on the host

citation:        SPLK-CL-000360 check text ("If the minPasswordDigit is missing or is
                 configured to 0, this is a finding") and fix text ("minPasswordDigit =
                 1"); authentication.conf.spec:468-476 (positive integer, default 0)
finding:         authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordDigit is absent or 0, so the
                 application accepts native account passwords with no numeric character.
